{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Surely</b> — for his image changes from day to day and from moment to moment, like the likeness of a flowing river whose image stands still." "And some say: כי בצלם — like צלמות. And the correct interpretation in my eyes: that man resembles an image, and just as the image changes, so he changes." "And the meaning of the image — the configurations of the celestial attendants and the uppermost stars, which do not stand still for a single moment on one arrangement, and the astrologers know this." "<b>And disquiets himself</b> — amassing money, like: ומי אוהב בהמון." "<b>He stores up</b> — little by little." "<b>And does not know who gathers them</b> — all of them in a single moment, at his death."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:16.730848601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}